Front-classify SINTERCARD's length-6 forms (frankenredis-ex3il)

sintercard_lim is my second-worst measured ratio against the incumbent: 0.7881
[0.7802, 0.8067]. The shape is `SINTERCARD 2 k1 k2 LIMIT n`, array length 6, and the
class stopped at arity 5 -- so every SINTERCARD carrying a LIMIT walked the cascade.

WHY THIS PATCH ADDS TWO PARSERS AND NOT ONE. Array length 6 admits BOTH readings:

    SINTERCARD 4 k1 k2 k3 k4          four plain keys
    SINTERCARD 2 k1 k2 LIMIT n        two keys with a LIMIT suffix

Widening the class while serving only the LIMIT form would drop the plain four-key
form on the generic path -- a NEW mis-claim, created by the fix, which is exactly the
defect opmo4 repaired in MGET. Both parsers pin their own `numkeys`, so at most one can
match a given packet and the chain order is immaterial.

THE EXECUTOR NEEDS NOTHING. execute_plain_sintercard_borrowed already takes a `tail`
slice and already implements the LIMIT suffix, including redis's rule that `LIMIT 0`
means NO LIMIT rather than "return nothing". This patch only builds the tails.

WHERE THE TOKEN CHECK LIVES, deliberately. `LIMIT` is verified in the parser, so a
packet the arm cannot serve declines before any executor work. That is the placement
that makes SINTERCARD's existing length-5 mis-claim cheap and ZDIFF's expensive
(frankenredis-nq6mh). The COUNT is NOT re-validated in the parser: the executor already
rejects negatives and treats 0 as no-limit, and duplicating that invites the two
copies to disagree.

HELD AS A PATCH, NOT APPLIED. /data is 53.4G against a 59G floor and has been below it
for four turns, so this cannot be compiled. An uncompiled edit in main.rs reddens every
pane's suite; an uncommitted one does not stay parked -- twice today one of mine was
swept into a peer's commit stripped of its caveats (frankenredis-fhgvc).

VERIFIED WITHOUT A COMPILER -- structural, not a type check:
    git apply --check                     rc=0
    brace delta, original vs patched      5 -> 5 unchanged
    paren delta                           2 -> 2 unchanged
    each new parser                       defined once, called once
    class widened 4..=5 -> 4..=6, old mint gone

THE GATE IS ALREADY IN, at 2978785dc. Note especially two rows there: `SINTERCARD 4
sc:1 sc:2 sc:3 sc:1` is the plain length-6 form this widening must NOT strand, and
`LIMIT 0` is the no-limit semantic a naive cap would break.

APPLY WITH:
    git apply scripts/sintercard_limit_classify.patch
    python3 scripts/build_preflight.py       # must print CLEAR TO BUILD
    cargo build --release -p fr-server --bin frankenredis --features perf-ab-cascade-bypass
    strings <binary> | grep -c FR_PERF_AB_CASCADE_BYPASS    # must be 1
    <three-way differ; SINTERCARD rows are already in the corpus>

NOT MEASURED. Predict the LEVEL, not a ratio (frankenredis-1t8c5): a classified route
reaches roughly 550 of dispatch. Do not carry ZRANGE's 0.8658 -> 1.1570 across; that
route paid the generic constant and this one pays a walk.

LEFT OUT: lengths 7 and up. Length 7 is ambiguous ((plain) x5 vs LIMIT x3) and would
need two more parsers; lengths 8 and 9 are unique LIMIT forms and safe, but each is a
separate claim deserving its own measurement rather than riding along unmeasured.

